-- title:
--   Kummer datum from an upper-triangular cocycle package
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative local ring, $p$ a prime with $p$ lying in the maximal ideal of $B$, and write $G_p$ for the group of $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphisms of `PadicAlgCl p`. Given functions $x, z : G_p \to B^\times$ and $y : G_p \to B$, an intermediate field $F$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, and assuming: $x$ and $z$ are multiplicative; $y(gh) = x(g)\,y(h) + y(g)\,z(h)$; for every $s \in G_p$ whose image under [`localGaloisToGlobal p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L41) (restrict scalars to $\mathbb{Q}$, then restrict to the normal subextension $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) fixes $F$ pointwise one has $x(s) = 1$, $y(s) = 0$, $z(s) = 1$; for all $g$ and all $n, a \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $g\mu = \mu^a$ for every $\mu$ with $\mu^{p^n} = 1$, the element $x(g)z(g) - a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$; and $z(g)^2 - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal for every $g$. Let further $\zeta$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity in `PadicAlgCl p`, $\Lambda$ an additive homomorphism from the residue field of $B$ to $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and $\eta \in B$. Then there exist $a \in \mathbb{Q}_p^\times$ and a unit $\alpha$ of `PadicAlgCl p` with $a = \alpha^p$ in `PadicAlgCl p` and $g\alpha = \zeta^{\,m(g)}\alpha$ for all $g \in G_p$, where $m(g)$ is the natural-number representative of $\Lambda$ applied to the residue class of $\eta\, y(g)\, z(g)^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the Kummer-theoretic extraction step for the off-diagonal entry of an upper-triangular local Galois package: the reduction of $y z^{-1}$ twisted by $\eta$ and pushed through $\Lambda$ is a $\mu_p$-valued $1$-cocycle trivial on a finite level, hence of the form $g \mapsto g\alpha/\alpha$ for a $p$-th root $\alpha$ of a $p$-adic unit; the proof cites [`groupCohomology.Kummer.exists_kummerCocycle_eq_of_isMulCocycle1_of_level`](thm.html#groupCohomology.Kummer.exists_kummerCocycle_eq_of_isMulCocycle1_of_level). It is used in the analysis of inertia for $p$-adic Galois representations, through [`GaloisRepAdic.exists_root_one_add_prime_inertia_sub_mem_of_quotientScalar_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.exists_root_one_add_prime_inertia_sub_mem_of_quotientScalar_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle).
